Project: Semester Project: Smart Parking Platform 

Version: 2.0  

Date: 09.017.2026  

  

1. Introduction  
 
WE ARE $oftware ¢orp. A fictitious software development studio with unlimited resources and budget. The project involves the planning and management of a software system that helps drivers locate, reserve, and pay for parking spaces for parking garages in real time. The platform will be available through web and mobile applications and will provide parking availability information, navigation assistance, and management tools for parking operators. The goal is to develop a project management plan for the creation of this system, including requirements gathering, stakeholder management, scheduling, budgeting, risk management, and team coordination. 
 
Aiming to do more than our competitors: 

 
Parknav® - Find Real Time On-Street and Off-Street Parking 

Just shows parking, cant pay for it ahead of time 
 
SpotHero | Get Everywhere Easier | Reserve Parking and Save 
Doesnt show a real time GPS or open parking, you need to know the address before hand 

 

Spot – Your Smart Parking Companion 
Has a waitlist to even join the app and not usable on non-mobile devices 
 
Download SpotHero - Find Parking for Android & iOS - Mobexer 
Known to only work in small towns with inaccurate pricing info, crashes unexpectedly. And slow support 

 

1.1 Purpose  

This document defines the requirements for Semester Project: Smart Parking Platform.  

1.2 Scope  

Drivers often spend significant time searching for available parking, leading to congestion, frustration, and lost productivity. Parking operators need better tools to monitor occupancy, manage pricing, and improve utilization of parking assets. 
 
Hopes to do all the competition can do and more 
 
 
Out of scope would be things that require more time such as:  

Communication with other customers through the app, making it a pseudo social media platform.  

 
It's own GPS system requiring dedicated owned satellites without connecting to others 

 

Extra addons without proper time slots 

 

Calling through the app without using the dedicated methods such as the customers' normal phone plan. 

 

 

2. Overall Description  

- Users: <List the different groups of users that will be using the finished product>  

- System Environment: Web-based / desktop / mobile application 

- Constraints: Must run on specific hardware, must require specific authentication, etc.  

- Assumptions: Application has internet / intranet access, etc. 

 

3. Functional Requirements  

The platform should provide: 

User registration and authentication 

Real-time parking space availability 

Interactive map displaying available parking locations 

Parking reservation capability 

Digital payment processing 

Reservation history and receipts 

Administrative dashboard for parking operators 

Occupancy reporting and analytics 

Notifications and alerts for users 

Integration with external mapping/navigation services 

 

  

4. Non-Functional Requirements  

NFR1: The system shall support at least 1,000 concurrent users.  

NFR2: The system shall update parking values within 1 second.  

NFR3: The system shall provide 99.99% uptime.  

NFR4: The system shall provide a visual parking gps/map 

NFR5: The system shall provide support lines for the app or dedicated parking area 

NFR6: The system shall be able to save info such as insurance info. 

NFR7: The system shall be able to save info such as roadside assistance info. 
   

5. Use Case Example  
 
Case 1: 

Title: Nearest parking search (GPS map) 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in, using search query in GPS 

Steps:  

1. User selects filters out the kind of parking they want  

2. User searches for said parking 

3. User views available parking 

4. User chooses the parking 

Postcondition: user has selected the parking they desire and can go to it or pay for it 

 

Case 2: 
Title: Nearest parking search (Catalogue grid) 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in, using search query in catalogue 

Steps:  

1. User selects filters out the kind of parking they want  

2. User searches for said parking 

3. User views available parking 

4. User chooses the parking 

Postcondition: user has selected the parking they desire and can go to it or pay for it 
 
Case 3: 
Title: creating an account 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User downloads the app or uses the website 

Steps:  

1.  User clicks "Sign up" 

2. User adds their email 

3. User verifies their email 

4. User creates their username and password 

5. User add two factor authentication (optional) 

6. User adds payment info during account creation to be saved to said account (optional)  

7. User inserts and saved driver information to their account 

Postcondition: user has created an account 

 
Case 4: 
Title: Adding/saves Payment info (internal, before parking) 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in, has payment info to save 

Steps:  

1. User selects the setting menu 

2. User selects payment options 

3. User puts in payment info with secure vendor/ or uses saved data on device 

4. User can use said info during parking 

Postcondition: user has saved a payment option to their account 
 
Case 5: 
Title: Adding/saves Payment info (internal, during parking) 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in, user has the parking they want to pay for in view 

Steps:  

1. User selects the parking 

2. User selects payment options 

3. User puts in payment info with secure vendor/ or uses saved data on device 

4. User pays for parking  

Postcondition: user has saved a payment option to their account 
 
Case 6: 
Title: Adding/saves insurance for ease of access (optional) 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in 

Steps:  

1. User selects the account 

2. User selects insurance info options 

3. User puts in insurance info with a printable file format 

4. User can view their insurance by going to their profile (local) 

Postcondition: user has saved their insurance files locally for ease of access 
 
 
Case 7: 
Title: Viewing parking history 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in 

Steps:  

1. User selects the account 

2. User selects "Parking History" 

3. User selects past parking from a list 

Postcondition: user will be able to view parking time, date, and payment history 

 
Case 8: 

Title: Reserving parking 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in, user has the parking they want to in view 

Steps:  

1. User selects the parking 

2. User selects payment options (optional based on vendor) 

3. User chooses to reserve the spot based on the vendor 

Postcondition: user has successfully reserved the parking (if allowed by the vendor) 

 
Case 9: 

Title: Locating route to parking Via GPS 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in, user has the parking they want in view 

Steps:  

1. User selects the parking 

2. User selects chooses routes based on filters such as tolls and time 

3. User can proceed to the parking via the route  

Postcondition: user has been routed to the chosen parking 

 
Case 10: 

Title: Add new vendors   

Actor: network admin, Cloud service 

Precondition: Vendor is locatable via the web/ database  

Steps:  

1. User selects available vendors 

2. User scans new vendor based on any database they may have 

3. User enters the vendor into the application via a dedicated dictionary/table  

4. User saves the new vendor with parking being updated for all users 

Postcondition: Mor parking/ vendors should show up in the application/ database 

 
Case 11: 
Title: Remove vendors   

Actor: network admin, Cloud service 

Precondition: Vendor is locatable via the web/ database  

Steps:  

1. User selects desired vendors from the database 

2. User removes said vendors 

Postcondition: the database should update removing the vendor and their parking  

 
Case 12: 

Title: Display unaffiliated Vendors   

Actor: network admin, Cloud service 

Precondition: Vendor is locatable via the web/ database  

Steps:  

1. User selects available vendors database 

2. User scans for available non associated parking vendors 

3. User chooses to toggle on the ability to use said vendors for the application 

Postcondition: More parking/ vendors should show up as unaffiliated in the application/ database (optional, client-side toggle for customers as well) 

 
Case 13: 

Title: Display unaffiliated Vendors   

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: user is logged in 

Steps:  

1. User selects the setting menu 

2. User scans for available non associated parking vendors 

3. User chooses to toggle on the ability to use said vendors for the application 

Postcondition: More parking/ vendors should show up as unaffiliated in the application/ database  

 
Case 14: 
Title: Save local cache and map 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: user is logged in has loaded a local map of available parking before 

Steps:  

1. User selects the setting menu 

2. User scans for available non associated parking vendors 

3. User saves a snapshot of local parking and their prices 

Postcondition: Parking should be saved locally in case the user loses access to internet. (note, values will not update) 

 
Case 15: 
Title: Call for roadside assistance 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: user is logged, user has saved roadside assistance info to their account 

Steps:  

1. User selects their profile 

2. User selects the insurance tab 

3. User selects the roadside assistance tab 

4. User can call for roadside assistance/ view their number (mobile only) 

5. User can send roadside assistance their location via text (mobile only) 

Postcondition: Roadside assistance will be notified 

 
Case 16: 

Title: Account deletion 

Actor: Customer 

Precondition: User is logged in 

Steps:  

1. User selects their profile 

2. User selects their profile settings 

3. User selects delete account 

4. User confirms account deletion after re logging the password and verifying through email 

Postcondition: The users account will be deleted. 
 

 
